      "totalDuration": "2 yrs 7 mos",
      "description": "Embarked as captain on a double-handed voyage aboard Ana María, a 30-year-old, 34-foot Pacific Seacraft, from the Salish Sea near Seattle to New Zealand. The journey was a profoundly transformative experience. Navigating the vast expanse of the Pacific Ocean, we adeptly managed serious medical emergencies, ranging from stomach viruses to broken bones–while engaging with foreign cultures. The experience honed my crew resource management skills, enabling me to effectively prioritize and focus on critical tasks when resources were limited. The lessons in leadership, teamwork, and resilience gleaned from this adventure are invaluable assets in my professional role as a software engineer. I welcome the opportunity to connect with fellow enthusiasts of sailing and technology.",
